.TH BROWSER-TAB 1
.SH NAME
browser\-tab \- browser\-tab — MCP server + CLI + TUI (single bin, subcommand dispatch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbrowser\-tab\fR [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
browser\-tab — MCP server + CLI + TUI (single bin, subcommand dispatch)
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-error output
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Log debug\-level info to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colors
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Run the MCP server (stdio default; \-\-http for Streamable HTTP)
.TP
\fBtui\fR
Launch the Ink TUI
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Run preflight checks (Node version, native module, config dir)
.TP
\fBrepl\fR
Interactive REPL driving the in\-process dispatcher
.RS
\fIAliases: \fRconsole
.RE
.TP
\fBhealth\fR
Print server health snapshot (calls health_check in\-process)
.TP
\fBnoop\fR
Demo: call the noop tool
.SH "BROWSER-TAB MCP"
Run the MCP server (stdio default; \-\-http for Streamable HTTP)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab mcp [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-http\fR
Use Streamable HTTP transport (requires MCP_HTTP_TOKEN)
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<port>\fR
HTTP port (default 8080)
.TP
\fB\-\-bind\fR \fI<host>\fR
HTTP bind addr (default 127.0.0.1)
.SH "BROWSER-TAB NOOP"
Demo: call the noop tool
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab noop [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<text>\fR
Input string to echo
.TP
\fB\-\-upper\fR
Return upper\-cased
